  {
   "slug": "weekly-box",
   "title": "The weekly box",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} --><p class=\"lead\">A box of the best seasonal fruit and vegetables from our growers, packed on Friday morning and ready for lunch.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns {\"align\":\"wide\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"price-tag\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group price-tag\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Small</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>For one or two people</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"price-from\"} --><p class=\"price-from\">$24</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"price-tag\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group price-tag\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Family</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>For three to five people</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"price-from\"} --><p class=\"price-from\">$38</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"price-tag\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group price-tag\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Fruit only</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Apples, pears, berries, plums</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"price-from\"} --><p class=\"price-from\">$18</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:group --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"chalkboard\",\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} --><div class=\"wp-block-group chalkboard\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} --><p class=\"eyebrow\">This week's box</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Week 44 · Small box</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"className\":\"price-list\"} --><ul class=\"wp-block-list price-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Vine tomatoes</strong> <span class=\"price\">500 g</span> <span class=\"desc\">Hal's polytunnel, the last of the season</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Rainbow carrots</strong> <span class=\"price\">1 kg</span> <span class=\"desc\">Muddy on purpose; they keep longer</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Cavolo nero</strong> <span class=\"price\">1 bunch</span> <span class=\"desc\">Strip the leaves, keep the stems for soup</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Cox apples</strong> <span class=\"price\">6</span> <span class=\"desc\">From the orchard at Millbrook End</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Victoria plums</strong> <span class=\"price\">500 g</span> <span class=\"desc\">Ripe now: eat within three days</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li><strong>Red onions</strong> <span class=\"price\">4</span> <span class=\"desc\">Dry-stored, lasts for weeks</span></li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --><!-- wp:buttons --><div class=\"wp-block-buttons\"><!-- wp:button --><div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"{{page:weekly-box}}\">Order by Wednesday noon</a></div><!-- /wp:button --></div><!-- /wp:buttons --></div><!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How it works</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Order or change your box by Wednesday at noon.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>We pack on Friday morning with whatever was picked that week.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Collect from the shop, or get free delivery within five miles.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Return the box and we will reuse it, again and again.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Allergies or strong dislikes? Tell us once and we will swap that item every week.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "featured_media": "weekly-box",
   "template": "page-full",
   "menu_order": 1
  },
  {
   "slug": "producers",
   "title": "Our producers",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} --><p class=\"lead\">Everything on our fresh shelves comes from within thirty miles. These are some of the people who grow, bake and make it.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":{{media_id:fields}},\"mediaType\":\"image\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"{{media:fields}}\" alt=\"Rows of crops\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:fields}} size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Riverside Growers</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Hal and his sister run eight acres on the river meadow: salad leaves, tomatoes, squash and the best leeks in the county. No-dig, no sprays, plenty of worms.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div><!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":{{media_id:orchard}},\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"mediaPosition\":\"right\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile has-media-on-the-right\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"{{media:orchard}}\" alt=\"Apple trees\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:orchard}} size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Millbrook End Orchard</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Noor looks after forty-two varieties of apples, pears and plums, some planted more than a century ago. Ask her about the russets.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div><!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":{{media_id:bread}},\"mediaType\":\"image\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"{{media:bread}}\" alt=\"Sourdough loaves\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:bread}} size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Night Owl Bakery</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Ilse's loaves ferment for thirty hours. She uses flour stone-ground at the mill two villages over.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div><!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":{{media_id:eggs}},\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"mediaPosition\":\"right\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile has-media-on-the-right\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"{{media:eggs}}\" alt=\"A tray of eggs\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:eggs}} size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Hilltop Hens</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Four hundred hens on rotating pasture, moved to fresh grass every week.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div><!-- /wp:media-text -->",
   "menu_order": 2
  },
  {
   "slug": "about",
   "title": "About the shop",
   "content": "<!-- wp:columns {\"align\":\"wide\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide\"><!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"50%\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:50%\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{media_id:hero-crate}},\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} --><figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"{{media:hero-crate}}\" alt=\"A crate of fresh vegetables\" class=\"wp-image-{{media_id:hero-crate}}\"/></figure><!-- /wp:image --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"50%\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:50%\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">A shop the village asked for</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Greenleaf began in 2017 as a trestle table at the Saturday market. When the old hardware shop on Orchard Row closed, two hundred neighbours lent us the money to open a proper grocery, and paid themselves back in vegetables.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Today we are a co-operative of growers, staff and customers. Profits go back into fair prices for farmers and the community fridge by the door.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Good food should travel by bicycle, not by plane.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Written on our first chalkboard</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Our promises</h2><!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Local first, organic always, imported only when nothing local exists</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>No plastic packaging on fresh produce</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Farmers paid within seven days</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list -->",
   "menu_order": 3
  },
  {
   "slug": "contact",
   "title": "Visit us",
   "content": "<!-- wp:columns {\"align\":\"wide\"} --><div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The shop</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>12 Orchard Row, Millbrook. Bike racks outside, two parking spaces behind the bakery.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Opening hours</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Monday – Saturday: 8 am – 7 pm</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Sunday: 9 am – 2 pm</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Farmers' market every Saturday on the green</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading --><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Get in touch</h2><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Phone <a href=\"tel:+15550135533\">+1 (555) 013-5533</a><br>Email <a href=\"mailto:hello@greenleaf.example\">hello@greenleaf.example</a></p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Wholesale enquiries from cafés and schools are very welcome.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->",
   "parent": "about",
   "menu_order": 4
  }
 ],
 "posts": [
  {
   "slug": "roast-squash-and-apple-soup",
   "title": "Roast squash and apple soup",
   "date": "2026-10-23T12:00:00",
   "excerpt": "Sweet squash, a sharp apple and a little chilli. Our favourite way to use this week's box.",
   "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>When the squash arrives in the boxes, this soup goes on the stove at the shop for staff lunch. The apple adds just enough sharpness to stop it feeling heavy.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:columns --><div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">You will need</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list --><ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>1 medium squash, in chunks</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>2 tart apples, quartered</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>1 red onion</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>1 litre of vegetable stock</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>A pinch of chilli flakes</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Olive oil, salt and pepper</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ul><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:column --><!-- wp:column --><div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} --><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Method</h3><!-- /wp:heading --><!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} --><ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Roast squash, apples and onion at 200°C for 40 minutes.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Scrape everything into a pan with the stock.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Simmer for 10 minutes, then blend until smooth.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item --><li>Season and finish with chilli and oil.</li><!-- /wp:list-item --></ol><!-- /wp:list --></div><!-- /wp:column --></div><!-- /wp:columns -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote --><blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Keep the squash seeds, toss them in oil and salt, and roast them for ten minutes. Best topping there is.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph --><cite>Hal, Riverside Growers</cite></blockquote><!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph --><p>Serves four, freezes beautifully, and tastes even better the next day with a thick slice of sourdough.</p><!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
   "categories": [
    "recipes"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "autumn",
    "vegetarian",
    "box-recipes"
   ],
   "featured_media": "orchard",
   "format": "standard",
   "sticky": true,
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": "Fern",
     "email": "fern@example.com",
     "content": "Made this last night with the family box. Kids asked for seconds!",
     "date": "2026-10-25T08:40:00"
    },
    {
     "author": "Greenleaf Market",
     "email": "greenleaf.market@example.com",
     "content": "Lovely to hear, Fern. Try it with a pear instead of apple next week.",
     "date": "2026-10-25T10:15:00"
    }
   ]
